  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759367,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 12 Years Later: A Chronicle of Oceania (Commodore 64)\n\nTen years have passed since Winston Smith’s rebellion. Oceania remains under the iron grip of the Party, but whispers of dissent stir in the shadows. *12 Years Later* plunges you into this bleak future as a new, unnamed protagonist – a former Inner Party member disillusioned by the regime's relentless control.\n\nNavigate the decaying, oppressive landscapes of London and beyond in this challenging platformer for the Commodore 64. Evade the ever-watchful eyes of the Thought Police, utilizing stealth and cunning to avoid capture. Collect fragments of forbidden knowledge – scraps of poetry, historical records, and subversive artwork – to piece together the truth about the Party’s lies and the fate of Winston Smith.\n\nGameplay blends classic platforming with puzzle elements, requiring careful timing and observation. Discover hidden passages, confront oppressive security measures, and make crucial choices that impact your survival and the potential for sparking a new flame of rebellion. Can you expose the Party’s secrets and offer a glimmer of hope to a broken society?"
    },
